WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:40.410
Katz disapproved of the fact
that Amuro refused to fight.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:46.720
He got in the Gundam Mk. II and tried
to face Rosamia Badam's Gaplant alone.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:53.630
However, he could have ended up dead had
Char and Kamille not come to assist him.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.460
Through the Haze of Darkness

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.550
We have transmission
from the relay station! Standby to copy.

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.250
Decryption code 22.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.020
Should the enemy proceed to fly over
the Pacific, cancel pursuit.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:24.030
- Your ship shall return to Kennedy...!
- That's enough!

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.620
Their plan is to make the Audhumla
cross the Pacific...

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.130
...and shoot them down from the Titans'
New Guinea base!

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.690
I know they've taken over Kennedy...

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:35.730
...but I'm not about to have some
Titans newcomer get all the credit!

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:38.710
Major.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.040
Will you change the message
in the communication capsule?

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:42.080
I'll do that.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:46.380
Tell the Murasame Laboratory in Japan
to watch for activities in New Guinea.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:50.710
Use the Newtype Laboratory's
encoding system.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.810
So that the Titans will be unable
to decipher it.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.080
Yes, sir!

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:56.750
Captain Wooder.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:59.130
How many mobile suits can we send out
right now?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.990
Six Hizacks and one Asshimar, sir!

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.060
- Send out the capsule!
- Yes, sir!

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:25.780
Will you be guiding us to Hickory?

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.780
That's precisely why I came here.

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:37.560
We've got to use this fog
and get at least...

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:40.530
...Kamille and Lieutenant Quattro
back to space.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:41.870
That's a responsibility of Karaba, right?

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.440
But you dislike fighting, don't you?

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:48.240
Naturally, I hate wars.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:52.950
But that's different from fighting
when one must fight.

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:55.250
You despise me, don't you?

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.320
I'm not that thickheaded.

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:05.330
For Amuro Ray, those seven
years were a period of sleep.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:09.360
The body must be cared for,
both physically and mentally.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:11.860
All you need to do is wake up.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.770
Then things will return
to the way they were.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.640
I don't have the confidence.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:21.370
You did in the past what Kamille
is doing now, right?

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:22.570
That's true, but...!

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:28.620
Beltorchika!

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:30.280
If you're feeling pity for me, forget it!

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:33.350
As I said, I'm not that thickheaded.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:39.260
If a woman can rouse a man to activity
by simply caressing him...

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:41.360
...then a woman will.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.720
Do you know why?

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.230
To test the man, right?

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.830
That's right.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.900
Because she wants the man
to be suitable for her.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.870
But once she finds that he's not,
she'll dump him.

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:53.910
There's no time for sympathy.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.200
You said you lost your parents
during the previous war.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.510
I'm a war orphan.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.240
I'm the one who wants sympathy.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:03.550
Sorry.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:11.050
We'll send Kamille and Lieutenant Quattro
back to space.

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:13.320
I might easily forget.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.730
I don't mind.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:21.290
Miss Beltorchika, Director Hayato
would like to see you.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.240
Thank you.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:25.770
I don't like that person.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:30.240
Could you leave a mobile suit behind?

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:31.510
Why's that?

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.410
Do you need a reason?

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:38.110
Sorry, but Kamille's a lot more accustomed
to the Mk. II. I cannot leave that behind.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:39.780
The Rick Dias would be fine.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:43.160
That model's developed by the A.E.U.G.
Leaving that behind is out of the question.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.990
You don't trust me, do you?

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:49.290
- Karaba won't be able to make use of it.
- I'll make them.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:53.760
The final battle between the A.E.U.G.
and Titans will take place in space.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.100
Why don't you...

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.280
Why don't you join us up in space?

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:05.480
I'd rather not.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:08.070
I'm terrified by that sense of no gravity.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.990
You're terrified to see Lalah, aren't you?

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:17.230
You believe you'll never meet
someone who has already passed away...

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:19.260
...but deep inside somewhere,
you believe you will.

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:20.420
That's what scares you.

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:21.900
No.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:26.670
During one's lifetime,
there are things one should do.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:30.100
And doing those things is the best tribute
to those who have died.

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:31.070
Stop talking!

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:37.800
<i>Char!</i>

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:41.880
<i>Lalah!</i>

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:57.520
Damn!

00:06:57.970 --> 00:06:59.160
Look at this!

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:02.300
This would make anyone angry,
not just your father.

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:03.430
I'm sorry.

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:05.410
You can't take me with you to space now,
can you?

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:06.600
We'll make it possible.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:08.570
Katz!

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:11.050
You're not planning to take off
without permission again, are you?

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.170
That never crossed my mind!

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:15.650
I just felt I should help
in anyway that I can.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:17.550
Kamille, bring down the crane!

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:18.790
Yes, sir!

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:21.550
I got permission from your father.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.990
What?! Really?!

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:26.660
Then I get to go to space, too?!

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:29.000
But I'm not going to be easy on you!

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:30.190
Of course not!

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:32.630
- That's great!
- Yes! Thank you very much!

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:35.000
What's wrong?

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:37.900
How about my father?
What does he plan to do?

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:42.740
He can't exactly ignore the task
of retaliating against the Titans.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:43.550
No, sir.

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:47.710
And he needs to be reachable
for your mother and siblings' sake.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:50.410
We'll make contact with Hickory.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:51.780
Right!

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.990
Amuro?

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:59.390
The clouds are thick along the coastline,
as always.

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:01.500
Anything?

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.130
No change in the amount of
Minovsky particles.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:07.260
We'll use the fog as cover and
arrive at Hickory as scheduled.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:08.100
Yes, sir!

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:10.160
But will we really be able to see Hickory?

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:13.340
The pigeon Beltorchika let go
should arrive at any time.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.570
We should see a signal.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:31.620
Now, that's a good bird.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.390
No change in the plan. Two mobile suits.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:39.830
Light fires along the runway
and send up flares!

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:40.600
Yes, sir!

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:43.830
No changes in plans
to dock with the Argama, are there?

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:47.930
No! This shuttle is capable of orbit
adjustments, so there won't be a problem!

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:55.490
Light fires along the runway!
Take up air defense positions!

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:05.730
Have I lost the bet with you, Captain?

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:06.460
Of course.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:10.160
The Audhumla will be sending pilots
to space from somewhere around here.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.470
There's no mistake! I've confirmed it twice!

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:26.140
Okay, we'll descend!

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:37.220
Want to descend in my mobile suit?

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:38.260
Yes!

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.020
Beltorchika!

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:45.730
I'll go to Hickory on Mr. Amuro's Rick Dias.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:47.500
Go ahead.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:49.030
Thank you very much.

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:52.040
You'd be a great help
if we can descend together.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.630
I can at least back you up.

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:54.680
Amuro!

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:56.740
I'll ride with you down to Hickory!

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:58.370
Sure, that'll be fine!

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:01.610
- Please guide us there!
- Sure!

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:12.590
Opening hatch!

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:15.030
Beltorchika, take off
when you see the next flash!

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:16.500
<i>Roger!</i>

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.700
Don't get your foot caught
in the linear seat's armrest.

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:23.740
Okay.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:26.070
Why didn't you ride with the Lieutenant?

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:30.670
I was happy to see that you decided
to ride a mobile suit, Mr. Amuro.

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:33.340
I hear Mr. Bright is on the Argama
that will be picking us up...

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.390
...so I want to tell him properly.

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:41.480
Did you see that flash directly below us?!

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:43.530
I sure did! Have the mobile suit unit
prepare for take-off!

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:47.520
Lower altitude!

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:49.890
The time has come.

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:50.900
Okay, Katz?

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:53.100
You do as Lieutenant Quattro tells you.

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:56.200
- <i>Take good care of Mother for me.</i>
- You don't have to tell me that!

00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:58.260
Amuro, make sure you don't get Katz hurt!

00:10:58.340 --> 00:10:59.140
<i>Roger!</i>

00:10:59.210 --> 00:10:59.970
Lieutenant Quattro.

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.270
Please take good care of him.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:04.080
<i>I think being a father figure will prove</i>
<i>to be a worthwhile experience for me.</i>

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:06.580
<i>I'm totally thrilled to do so.</i>

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:09.520
- I hope it proves to be worthwhile!
- <i>Thank you!</i>

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:19.360
Okay!

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:24.260
- Feeling okay?
- I'm okay.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:37.080
The enemy!

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:38.110
Enemy?!

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:40.380
They haven't noticed us yet.

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.420
Shouldn't we let Lieutenant Quattro know?!

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:45.480
If you want to go to space, keep quiet!

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:51.230
I can see the runway!

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:56.970
In a place like this?

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:18.950
Lieutenant Quattro! I'm landing!

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.350
Go ahead!

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:22.120
It looks like Amuro's Rick Dias is lost.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:24.860
It's a Hyaku Shiki and Gundam!

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.330
That's strange. Where's Amuro?

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:35.530
<i>Lieutenant Quattro!</i>

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.140
I'm Quattro Bajeena!
Sorry to put you through the trouble!

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.670
Welcome to Hickory!

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:46.550
Please hurry and load your mobile suits
onto the shuttle!

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.850
We'd also like to load a Rick Dias.
Can we get that onto the shuttle, too?

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:52.690
The Hyaku Shiki is the A.E.U.G.'s
newly produced mobile suit!

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:55.750
The Argama's orders are
to return that at any cost!

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:57.820
- The Argama's orders?
- Yes!

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:06.540
They've found us!

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:08.940
- Descend! But no closer to Hickory!
- Right!

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.700
It's only a matter of time!

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:17.870
The fact that they're not sending
mobile suits out...

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:19.920
...is perhaps a sign that they've already
unloaded them.

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:26.050
- Are you okay?
- Don't worry about me. Just get them!

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:33.890
- All right!
- That was luck!

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:43.060
It's coming!

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:48.700
Come out front! Grab onto my knee!

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:51.900
- Where's the Audhumla?
- It's keeping a distance from Hickory.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.150
Can't we get our mobile suits out?!

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:58.480
Two units launching now.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:01.680
Send unmanned units out on Dodais!
They'll act as decoys!

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:02.950
I'll leave you in charge here!

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:05.430
- Where to?!
- To the mobile suit deck!

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:08.030
Hurry with the Gundam, too!
What's the delay?!

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:11.190
It's not time yet, is it?!

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.770
We have less than five minutes!
Load the Gundam!

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.170
There's one more person
we want to send to space!

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:17.210
I'll go get him!

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:21.210
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:23.840
Should anything happen, at least take
the Hyaku Shiki back to space!

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:26.770
- Dislodge the joints!
- Can't do that!

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:33.920
Over there?

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:36.080
They should be commencing countdown
anytime now.

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:38.320
But Amuro's battling
with Katz still on board.

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:49.040
The Rick Dias?!

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:50.070
Amuro!

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:51.700
How the...?!

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.000
Go down!

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:56.480
I-I'm falling!

00:14:57.150 --> 00:14:59.080
Why haven't you landed?!

00:14:59.150 --> 00:15:00.380
<i>Katz is still aboard with you, right?!</i>

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:03.040
The countdown should be starting now!
What are you going to do?!

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:05.010
Forget about it, Amuro.

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:06.320
Nonsense!

00:15:06.390 --> 00:15:07.860
There's still time!

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:09.410
<i>There should be about four or five minutes!</i>

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:11.760
Where's Hickory?!

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:13.590
<i>To your left, below!</i>

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:14.630
There?

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:21.130
A farewell gift.
I'm sure it'll come in handy.

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:22.170
Amuro.

00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:26.540
I used this gun to exchange shots
against Zeon's Char...

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:28.310
...during the One Year War.

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:31.470
But this must be very valuable to you.

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:33.380
You want to be a pilot, right?

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:34.640
Yes.

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:39.820
Amuro!

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:41.290
Has Kamille been detected by the Sudori?!

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:43.950
Considering this fog, he should be okay!

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:45.620
Please take Katz!

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:48.060
I don't want to give Hayato
another reason to laugh at me!

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.530
All is for naught
if the shuttle gets blown up!

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:53.430
<i>I'll protect it!</i>

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:56.840
As for you, I'm sure you have a million
things to do in outer space, Lt. Quattro!

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:59.610
But we still need to get Kamille on board.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:01.030
Katz!

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:04.100
Lieutenant Quattro, you're
extremely important to the A.E.U.G..

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:06.050
Amuro! Please protect the shuttle!

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:09.810
Hurry! To the cockpit!

00:16:09.890 --> 00:16:12.650
Watch out, it might go off,
since I'm not used to holding one!

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:13.980
Very well.

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:17.550
We'll count on Kamille and Amuro
to protect the shuttle.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:25.500
How obedient.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:34.940
If you send it out directly,
it'll hit the enemy!

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.910
Don't take them lightly
just because they're unmanned!

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:41.040
Please, get at least one!

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:48.480
Is the Audhumla under attack?

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:50.050
Yes, but only against a few.

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:51.750
These old shuttles pull a lot of Gs.

00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:52.890
I know!

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:55.300
Guns won't fire with the safety catch on.

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:58.060
All we can do now is pray to the heavens.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:16:59.800
Take good care of that gun.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:00.660
Yes.

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:02.710
Countdown, 180!

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:05.330
- Aren't you scared?
- No!

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:07.410
I'm scared.

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:09.500
I'd rather be moving about.
It's a lot less scary.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:13.340
That's not Beltorchika!

00:17:15.150 --> 00:17:16.080
Gotcha, Gundam!

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:20.690
Go down!

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:25.020
It's the end of the road for you.

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:28.430
At times like this, the Asshimar is
the better bet for its superior mobility!

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:37.740
Kamille! Stay focused!

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:38.970
Can you hear me?!

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:40.910
Mr. Amuro? Where's Katz?!

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:42.310
<i>I'm returning him to space!</i>

00:17:46.350 --> 00:17:48.280
You're not going to make it!

00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:49.780
Remain by my side until your next chance!

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:51.290
Roger that!

00:17:51.350 --> 00:17:52.790
The enemy before us is very dangerous!

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:55.620
Beltorchika must be headed
for the Audhumla!

00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:58.320
How could he think of a woman
at a time like this?

00:17:58.400 --> 00:18:01.660
<i>Kamille! Ahead of you, slightly below!</i>
<i>Use your bazooka!</i>

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:04.660
Where is it?! I can't see it!

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:05.890
<i>Fire!</i>

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:10.170
You won't hit me!

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:11.040
A bit lower!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.580
We've received the Argama's
laser transmission.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:20.010
They're responding.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:26.750
Tell Lieutenant Quattro that Karaba
will put the Rick Dias and Mk. II to good use!

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:28.210
Roger!

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.990
Countdown, 95!

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:33.090
The Audhumla?!

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:34.530
Oh no!

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:39.700
The countdown should've started by now!

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:42.070
Just a bit longer. Kamille!

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:50.450
Where are the others?

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:56.450
He's severed just the backpack!

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:57.710
Amuro Ray did?!

00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:00.450
Beltorchika! Proceed onto the Audhumla!
You're in the way!

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:03.290
- Retrieve the Comet!
- Yes, sir!

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:05.190
Descend as soon as we retrieve her!

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:07.130
- We'll head out to the ocean!
- Yes, sir!

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:18.870
Is that it?!

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:24.240
Was that Dodai a decoy?

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:28.050
You're even sending these out?

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:36.150
I hit the cockpit!

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:40.260
Is it the Rick Dias?!

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:43.390
Pay attention to your back, too!

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:48.670
Kamille Bidan. He's not going to make it.

00:19:48.740 --> 00:19:52.000
No, but like you, he will eventually return.

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:56.770
Mr. Amuro! It's impossible!
We're practically skimming the ground!

00:19:57.310 --> 00:19:59.080
The enemy's lost some of its power!

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:00.170
Press him! Watch!

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:10.490
The Asshimar's flying abilities
won't be bothered by this!

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:11.460
Not by this!

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:13.360
Kamille! Fire!

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:21.200
Kamille! Escape!

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:25.070
I'm taking you with me!

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:26.470
He's got me!

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:39.160
We're lifting off!

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:43.050
My Asshimar!

00:20:59.540 --> 00:21:01.100
Where's Amuro's Rick Dias?!

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:04.840
It's all right. Hickory's crew has rescued him.

00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:08.280
Mr. Amuro... is okay, isn't he?

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:10.690
He's quite a guy.

00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:12.310
I saw it, too.

00:21:12.390 --> 00:21:14.220
I have to change my opinion of him.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.720
Yes, you may have to.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:18.260
Amuro Ray has awoken
from his long sleep.

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:24.060
I dislike frightened men,
but war-like men are just as bad.

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:30.440
I'd like to believe that he's a Newtype.

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:31.500
- Same here.
- He's here!

00:21:46.190 --> 00:21:47.050
Amuro! Amuro!

00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:48.950
Thank you, Beltorchika.

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:50.820
There's nothing to cry about.

00:21:50.890 --> 00:21:53.560
But... But, Amuro...!

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:56.450
Kamille, I apologize.

00:21:56.930 --> 00:21:58.330
I should be thanking you.

00:21:58.400 --> 00:21:59.890
Captain Amuro Ray.

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:00.490
No problem.

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:02.470
Hey, information from Kai?

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:05.370
Yes, but we can't relay messages any more...

00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:08.480
...so you'd be wise to depart
from the American continent.

00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:09.450
I agree.

00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:11.310
Have you contacted
Luio & Company in Hong Kong?

00:22:11.380 --> 00:22:12.780
We can't from Hickory.

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:14.320
I understand. We'll do it ourselves.

00:22:14.380 --> 00:22:17.010
- Thank you.
- I'll excuse myself.

00:22:17.090 --> 00:22:18.990
It's from Kai.

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:21.280
Shall I open it?

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:22.320
Please.

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:25.960
Outer space.

00:22:27.100 --> 00:22:29.060
I wonder how Fa's doing?

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:49.720
The mobile suit departing from Japan
is a new enemy.

00:23:49.790 --> 00:23:52.690
Its pilot is Four Murasame.

00:23:52.930 --> 00:23:56.990
Amuro soon realizes that Four
is unlike any enemy in the past.

00:23:57.060 --> 00:23:59.760
Meanwhile, he has a reunion
with Mirai and her children.

00:23:59.830 --> 00:24:02.530
And he finds himself annoyed
with Kamille's fighting style.

00:24:03.140 --> 00:24:07.570
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Hong Kong City".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Hong Kong City

00:24:08.040 --> 00:24:12.670
You will see the tears of time.
